<script>
  $(document).ready(function() {
    $('#loading').show();
    setTimeout(function() {
      $('#loading').hide();
      $('#finish').show();
    }, 5000);
  });
</script>

<div class="practice-page">
  <a href="/dynamic_loading" class="back-link">← Back to Dynamic Loading</a>
  <h1 class="practice-title">Dynamic Loading — Example 3</h1>
  <div class="practice-banner"><ul>
    <li>The page auto-loads after 5 seconds — no button needed</li>
    <li>Wait for the spinner to disappear, then assert the login form is visible</li>
    <li>Use credentials: <strong>tomsmith</strong> / <strong>SuperSecretPassword!</strong></li>
  </ul></div>

  <h4>Example 3: Element hidden, becomes visible after 5 seconds</h4>

  <div id="loading" style="margin-top:1rem;">Loading... <img src="/img/ajax-loader.gif"></div>

  <div id="finish" style="display:none; margin-top:1rem; max-width:420px;">
    <h4>Hello World!</h4>
    <p style="color:#64748b; font-size:0.85rem; margin-bottom:1rem;">Enter <em>tomsmith</em> / <em>SuperSecretPassword!</em></p>
    <form name="login" id="login" action="/secure_dynamic_loading" method="post">
      <div style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
        <label for="username" style="font-weight:600; display:block; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">Username</label>
        <input type="text" class="form-control" id="username" name="username" style="width:100%; padding:0.5rem; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius:6px;" />
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
        <label for="pwd" style="font-weight:600; display:block; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">Password</label>
        <input type="password" class="form-control" id="pwd" name="password" style="width:100%; padding:0.5rem; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius:6px;" />
      </div>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" style="padding:0.6rem 1.5rem;">Submit</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>
